1
00:00:00,554 --> 00:00:02,107
The shutters are down.

2
00:00:02,107 --> 00:00:04,048
The spreadsheets are still open.

3
00:00:04,048 --> 00:00:09,093
Stock, deliveries, invoices: one more evening
spent looking for the small thing that

4
00:00:09,093 --> 00:00:10,646
could go wrong tomorrow.

5
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:17,338
This fictional shop has sixty products, twelve
suppliers, and ninety days of sales.

6
00:00:17,338 --> 00:00:19,195
Twelve review candidates surface.

7
00:00:19,955 --> 00:00:21,829
Original files stay intact.

8
00:00:21,829 --> 00:00:26,045
Confirmed mappings and recorded hashes keep
every flag traceable.

9
00:00:26,652 --> 00:00:30,600
Stock cover compares recent sales with
supplier lead time.

10
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:34,548
The lowest cover comes first, with estimates
clearly marked.

11
00:00:35,304 --> 00:00:38,946
A short inbox replaces the hunt across rows.

12
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:42,002
Oat milk has four units left.

13
00:00:42,002 --> 00:00:47,884
A hundred and seventy-four sales over ninety
days gives just over two days of cover.

14
00:00:48,651 --> 00:00:50,519
The supplier needs five days.

15
00:00:50,519 --> 00:00:55,004
But missing sales count as zero, and incoming
orders still need checking.

16
00:00:55,004 --> 00:00:56,499
The assumptions stay visible.

17
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,628
Now Ministral reads the evidence locally.

18
00:00:59,628 --> 00:01:03,269
It explains the flag and proposes a next step.

19
00:01:03,269 --> 00:01:08,125
Source and number checks help, but the wording
still needs human judgement.

20
00:01:09,453 --> 00:01:15,047
The proposed next step becomes a purchase
review draft, ready for an owner to inspect.

21
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:19,594
Review the wording, verify the sources, and
edit where needed.

22
00:01:19,594 --> 00:01:24,146
The model helps write the request; it does not
make the decision.

23
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:28,768
Approval makes the draft available for export.

24
00:01:28,768 --> 00:01:34,113
It sends no email, places no order, and
changes no financial record.

25
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:40,528
The audit trail records the check, model
explanation, approval, and export.

26
00:01:40,528 --> 00:01:42,246
Each step stays accountable.

27
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,437
In this synthetic run, thousands of rows
become twelve candidates and one approved

28
00:01:48,437 --> 00:01:48,855
draft.

29
00:01:48,855 --> 00:01:52,619
Actual owner time savings still need a field
study.

30
00:01:52,619 --> 00:01:54,292
Catch the small things.

31
00:01:54,292 --> 00:01:55,547
Keep your evening.
